language ESSENCE' 1.0
$ Put the balls 1 to n into c boxes so that no triple of balls x, y, z with x + y = z is all in one box (Schur's lemma).
given n : int(1..)
given c : int(1..)
$ balls[i] is the box holding ball i
find balls : matrix indexed by [int(1..n)] of int(1..c)

branching on [balls]
such that
$ for every triple of balls x, y, z with x + y = z (z at most n), the three balls are not all in the same box
forAll x : int(1..n) . forAll y : int(1..n-x) . forAll j : int(1..c) . (!(balls[x] = j /\ balls[y] = j /\ balls[x+y] = j))
